  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2ee87e681215b6147a44021cf30db039, type: 3}
  m_Name: 4.Archbishop's Palace
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  nameOfPoint: Archbishop's Palace
  coordinatesPoint: {x: 14.512969, y: 35.900784}
  firstPartInfo: "At the Archbishop\u2019s Palace, I ask for any records of Jewish
    families dating before 1950. As I am rummaging through the files, I also encounter
    another conflict between Christianity and Judaism stemming from this palace.
    Although not much information remains about this situation, I do find the remains
    of a blood libel pamphlet accusing Jewish residents of Malta of harming Christians
    to perform their rituals. No court cases or police reports are connected to this
    pamphlet\u2019s accusations, just this solitary flimsy piece of paper scattered
    amongst other records."
  secondPartInfo: "Focusing on my research about the Tayar family, I search for the
    Tayar name and come across a story concerning Ondina\u2019s elder brother, Oscar.
    It so happened that he fell in love with an eighteen-year-old Christian Maltese
    girl. This caused turmoil on both sides as they were not comfortable with mixing
    religious beliefs to that social extent. Oscar was scolded by his mother, while
    the young girl was taken to the Archbishop\u2019s Palace and was harshly reminded
    of the fear of eternal damnation. This situation set up a barrier between Oscar
    and his mother, Rachele. She would later be bedridden for a year, with the cause
    being attributed to the emotional turmoil of the situation, while Oscar would
    emigrate to Australia. \r\n\r\nAs I am delving through the Archbishop\u2019s
    Palace\u2019s records, I find that a complaint had been made about two children
    disturbing a procession further down Old Mint Street. Their resolution reminds
    me of the Tayar siblings.\r"
  imgMarker: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c98feaebd40d8df449e6d3855ac84352, type: 3}
  imgMain: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f26fa8880b3aeef4b8516c82dc12f2a5, type: 3}
  nameOfStory: Jewish
  hintOfPOI: 'The Tayar family might have been living at Old Mint Street. Solution
    (streetwise kid): My grandmother once told me about some naughty children living
    further down Old Mint Street.'
  solutionOfPOI: My grandmother once told me about some naughty children living further
    down Old Mint Street.
